%% DM26-0670

%% A workload of many pods at once, as built (2026-11-04, docs/architecture/authority-model.md, "Multi-instance workloads", built 2026-11-01). One catalog entry, one identity
%% and one escrow key, with each pod its own instance. Its first user is the load harness.
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant Cat as Catalog (instances: "many")
    participant A as pod A
    participant B as pod B
    participant CA as Credentials agent
    participant CI as cert-issuer
    participant Bk as Cassini broker
    participant Sub as a subscriber

    Cat->>CA: applying the catalog signs it off: one workload, one ServiceAccount, one identity
    par each pod asks with its own token, as any workload does (general/workload_certificate_issuance)
        A->>CA: issuance, the token bound to pod A's UID
        CA->>CI: /internal/issue
        CI-->>A: a certificate naming the identity, i:uid:(A's UID) and i:pod:(A's name)
    and
        B->>CA: issuance, the token bound to pod B's UID
        CA->>CI: /internal/issue
        CI-->>B: the same identity, i:uid:(B's UID) and i:pod:(B's name)
    end
    Note over CA: A reissue revokes the certificate it supersedes per (identity, instance), so A's does not end B's. Nothing about an instance is self-reported.

    opt the workload has encryption: one key per workload, shared by its instances
        A->>CA: A's custodian: X's escrow key: none yet, so it is issued one and stores it
        B->>CA: B's custodian asks meanwhile
        CA-->>B: BeingIssued: only one first issuance per identity, so it asks again
        B->>CA: asks again, once it is escrowed
        CA-->>B: the same key, sealed to B's ephemeral, into B's own custody slot
        Note over A,B: A secret sealed to the workload opens in any instance. A reply for one pod is sealed to a key made for that one exchange.
    end

    A->>Bk: register. The broker reads the instance from the leaf
    B->>Bk: register. Two sessions: supersede is by (identity, instance)
    A->>Bk: publish
    Bk->>Sub: delivery, published_by the identity and published_instance A, both from the verified certificate

    alt pod A restarts in place: the same UID, a new key
        A->>Bk: register under its own instance
        Bk->>Bk: it supersedes its own older session, and only that (broker/session_supersede_takeover)
    else pod A shuts down cleanly
        A->>Bk: the builder's drain says goodbye
        Bk->>Bk: its session ends at once
    else pod A dies uncleanly
        Bk->>Bk: its session is detached for the retention window, and no successor supersedes it
    end
    Note over Bk,Sub: Pods are not a consumer group. A topic delivers to every subscriber, so this serves publishers and does not share work.
